   "id": "p0",
   "type": "photo",
   "render": "editorial",
   "at": "08:30",
   "slides": [
    {
     "t": "cover",
     "kicker": "Navratri · Day 1 · Pratipada",
     "title": "Ghatasthapana at home, step by step",
     "bn": "ঘরেই ঘটস্থাপনা",
     "sub": "The first-day kalash ritual, the simple way",
     "photo": {
      "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/Navratri_Kalash_Puja.jpg",
      "artist": "Ashish Suryavanshi858",
      "license": "CC0",
      "cx": 0.5,
      "cy": 0.5
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "list",
     "kicker": "What you need",
     "title": "Keep these ready",
     "bn": "যা যা লাগবে",
     "items": [
      [
       "A kalash of clay, brass or copper",
       "ঘট"
      ],
      [
       "A clay tray, clean soil and barley",
       "মাটি আর যব"
      ],
      [
       "Five mango or ashoka leaves",
       "আমপাতা"
      ],
      [
       "A whole coconut in red cloth",
       "নারকেল"
      ],
      [
       "Red thread, roli and rice",
       "লাল সুতো, সিঁদুর, আতপ চাল"
      ],
      [
       "Ganga water or clean water",
       "গঙ্গাজল"
      ],
      [
       "A coin, a betel nut, durva",
       "পয়সা, সুপুরি, দূর্বা"
      ],
      [
       "The Goddess's picture, a ghee lamp, incense, flowers",
       "দেবীর ছবি, প্রদীপ, ধূপ, ফুল"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Step 1",
     "num": 1,
     "title": "Find the muhurta",
     "bn": "শুভ সময় দেখে নিন",
     "body": "Look up Pratipada and the ghatasthapana window for your city in your local panchang, or ask your family priest. Most families set up the kalash in the morning."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Step 2",
     "num": 2,
     "title": "Sow the barley",
     "bn": "মাটিতে যব ছড়ান",
     "body": "Clean the puja corner and set a low stool with a red cloth. Spread clean soil in the clay tray, scatter barley seeds, cover them lightly and sprinkle water. They will sprout over the nine days."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Step 3",
     "num": 3,
     "title": "Prepare the kalash",
     "bn": "ঘট সাজান",
     "body": "Draw a swastika on it with roli and tie red thread round its neck. Fill it with water, a little Ganga water, a coin, a betel nut and a few grains of rice.",
     "photo": {
      "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/Arcana_Plate_for_Worship.jpg",
      "artist": "Vish79",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "cx": 0.5,
      "cy": 0.55
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Step 4",
     "num": 4,
     "title": "Leaves, coconut, and in place",
     "bn": "আমপাতা আর নারকেল",
     "body": "Arrange five mango leaves in the mouth with the tips outward and rest the coconut on them. Set the kalash on the barley tray, in front of the Goddess's picture."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Step 5",
     "num": 5,
     "title": "Make your sankalpa",
     "bn": "সংকল্প করুন",
     "body": "Light the lamp and incense. Holding water, rice and a flower, say your name, the occasion and your wish to worship the Goddess for these nine days. Your own words are enough.",
     "bn_body": "নিজের ভাষাতেই বলুন: আপনি কে, কোন উপলক্ষ্যে, কী প্রার্থনা।"
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Every day",
     "num": 6,
     "title": "For the nine days",
     "bn": "ন'দিন রোজ",
     "body": "Offer flowers, a lamp and fruit each day, and sprinkle a little water on the barley. After Navami, retire the kalash gently and pour its water at the roots of a plant."
    },
    {
     "t": "end",
     "title": "Save this for Pratipada morning",
     "bn": "পরিবারের গ্রুপে পাঠিয়ে দিন",
     "ask": "Save it · send it to the family group"
    }
   ],
   "caption": {
    "en": "Navratri and Durga Puja 2026 at home: ghatasthapana step by step, the way Kolkata families do it 🪔\n\nEverything you need, then the kalash, the barley, the sankalpa and what to do each of the nine days. Customs differ from family to family, so follow yours where it's different, and check today's muhurta in your local panchang.\n\nSave this for tomorrow morning, and tell us: does your family set up a ghat? 👇",
    "keywords": [
     "navratri 2026",
     "ghatasthapana",
     "kalash sthapana",
     "ghatasthapana vidhi at home",
     "navratri puja at home",
     "durga puja at home"
    ],
    "tags": "#Navratri2026 #DurgaPuja2026 #Navratri"
   }
