   "at": "12:30",
   "slides": [
    {
     "t": "cover",
     "kicker": "Navadurga · Day 1 of 9",
     "title": "Shailaputri, daughter of the mountain",
     "bn": "মা শৈলপুত্রী",
     "sub": "The first form of Durga, worshipped on Pratipada",
     "photo": {
      "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/55/Idol_of_Navadurga_during_Durga_Puja_2024_at_Paltan_Bazar_Durga_Mandir%2C_Dibrrugarh_01.jpg",
      "artist": "AjayDas",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "cx": 0.5,
      "cy": 0.4
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Who she is",
     "title": "Parvati, born to the Himalaya",
     "bn": "হিমালয়-কন্যা",
     "body": "Shaila means mountain and putri daughter. She is Parvati as the daughter of Himavat, king of the Himalayas, and in many tellings Sati reborn. Her day begins Navratri, together with ghatasthapana."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "How she is shown",
     "title": "Bull, trident, lotus, moon",
     "bn": "বৃষবাহিনী",
     "body": "She rides a bull and holds a trident in one hand and a lotus in the other, with a crescent moon on her head. She stands for steadiness: the root from which the rest of Navratri grows."
    },
    {
     "t": "mantra",
     "kicker": "Shailaputri dhyana mantra",
     "script": "deva",
     "text": "वन्दे वाञ्छितलाभाय चन्द्रार्धकृतशेखराम् ।\nवृषारूढां शूलधरां शैलपुत्रीं यशस्विनीम् ॥",
     "translit": "Vande vanchhita labhaya chandrardha krita shekharam, vrisharudham shuladharam shailaputrim yashasvinim",
     "meaning": "I bow to the glorious Shailaputri, who grants what we wish for, who wears the half-moon on her head, rides a bull and holds a trident.",
     "meaning_bn": "অর্ধচন্দ্রশোভিতা, বৃষবাহিনী, ত্রিশূলধারিণী মা শৈলপুত্রীকে প্রণাম।"
    },
    {
     "t": "list",
     "kicker": "Today",
     "title": "Day 1 at a glance",
     "bn": "প্রথম দিন",
     "items": [
      [
       "Form: Shailaputri",
       "শৈলপুত্রী"
      ],
      [
       "Ritual: ghatasthapana",
       "ঘটস্থাপনা"
      ],
      [
       "Common offering: ghee",
       "ঘি"
      ],
      [
       "Short mantra: Om Devi Shailaputryai Namah",
       "ওঁ দেবী শৈলপুত্র্যৈ নমঃ"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "end",
     "title": "Nine forms, nine days. Follow along.",
     "bn": "কাল: মা ব্রহ্মচারিণী",
     "ask": "Follow for all nine days"
    }
   ],
   "caption": {
    "en": "Navratri Day 1 of the Durga Puja 2026 countdown: Maa Shailaputri 🙏\n\nThe first of the nine forms of Durga: who she is, how she is shown, and her dhyana mantra with its meaning. In Kolkata the big pujo starts on Shashthi, but many Bengali homes light the ghat from today.\n\nSave the mantra for your morning puja, and send it to someone keeping all nine days 🙏",
